    "body": "> […] has to be either a person or a company.\r\n\r\nOr person**s**, plural, as is the case with Starship. As far as I could find, you do not have a CLA that assigns contributors’ copyright over to you. So, as an example, the commit aceda0052f7e946d9c43afad5ae440af3e6cd43e was not authored by you and someone else holds the copyrights. (Disclaimer: if the code in that commit is enough to qualify the author for copyright, that is for legal to figure out 🤷‍♀)\r\n\r\nThis is why you will see projects that do not work with copyright assignments state that the copyrights are held by the contributors, often with a link to [the contributors graph](https://github.com/starship/starship/graphs/contributors).",
